# LazyTrails context-ignore policy template
# Target path: .codexignore
# Purpose: guide agents away from high-cost, generated, secret, binary, and archive paths.
# This is an agent context policy, not a substitute for .gitignore or security review.
.git/
node_modules/
vendor/
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/
coverage/
.next/
.vite/
.cache/
logs/
*.log
tmp/
temp/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
*.pem
*.key
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.svg
*.pdf
*.zip
*.mp4
.lazytrails/state/archive/
.lazytrails/sessions/archive/
# Package reference folders are governed by .lazytrails/load-map.yml, not hard context-ignore entries, so explicit workflow reads remain possible.
# Lockfile special case: list lockfile paths by default, but do not read full contents unless dependency, supply-chain, vulnerability, reproducibility, installer, package-manager migration, or explicitly requested.
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
bun.lockb
poetry.lock
uv.lock
Cargo.lock
go.sum
